     service label (Bakery, Seafood, Business Center, Pharmacy) prints on
     the staff side, and every non-service label (Market, Produce,
     Kitchen, Apparel, Baby) prints on the shopping floor. 114 m^2 with
     zero fixtures inside. The 30 pt south mouth is the staff way in.
  2. **NE slot left walkable** (x 1073-1089, y 64-118, 2.3 x 7.7 m).
     Accepted, not a finding: no drawn casework, no door, aisle-width,
     open to the aisle-21 end of the top action alley, and it holds no
     product either way. Leaving it green is the direction that cannot
     hide shopping floor.
  3. **far_snaps** re-derived: PHARMACY DRIVE-THRU 25.9 m is forced (the
     label prints at (1158,757), outside the boundary); SEAFOOD 4.5 m and
     BAKERY 3.8 m are the expected consequence of correctly sealing those
